Mapping
Id	Rule	Status	Derived from	Module
M1	the input is an OTLP JSON Lines file; TracesData and LogsData carry the eight, MetricsData none	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP file; Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes	integrations/otlp_json
M2	lines are read in the file's order; nothing is sorted	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP file	integrations/otlp_json
M3	fields with unknown names are ignored	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP JSON	integrations/otlp_json
M4	ids are written as their hex text and compared without regard to case	derived	Content › Integrations › OTLP JSON	integrations/otlp_json
M5	the eight are found by their attribute keys, structured or as a JSON string	derived	Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes; the eight GenAI set artefacts	integrations/otlp_json
M6	each of the eight has sheets of its own; input and output messages are kept apart	derived	the eight GenAI set artefacts	system_instructions; tool_definitions; input_messages; output_messages; tool_call_arguments; tool_call_result; memory_records; retrieval_documents; parts
M7	a schema definition with fields of its own is a sheet of its own	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (same domains); Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes (fields)	system_instructions; tool_definitions; input_messages; output_messages; tool_call_arguments; tool_call_result; memory_records; retrieval_documents; parts
M8	a nonsimple field is a child sheet carrying its parent's key	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (nonsimple domain; normalization)	relations
M9	every row of the eight carries its span's traceId and spanId	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (normalization); Content › Integrations › OTLP records	relations
M10	a value of any shape is one sheet whose rows refer to their parent row	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (foreign key to its own relation)	relations
M11	order is kept as position columns in the key	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (rows unordered); Content › Integrations › JSON (arrays ordered); Content › Integrations › GenAI input messages (order)	relations
M12	an enum is a simple value, so a column	derived	Content › Integrations › relations (simple domain)	system_instructions; tool_definitions; input_messages; output_messages; tool_call_arguments; tool_call_result; memory_records; retrieval_documents; parts
M13	properties beyond a schema go to their object's value sheet	derived	Content › Integrations › GenAI structured attributes (further properties); M10	relations
M14	numbers are written as the source writes them	derived	Content › Integrations › JSON (range and precision may be limited)	relations
M15	values MTSV cannot represent are not written	derived	Content › Format › fields and sheet names	relations
M16	sheet and column names are the source's own; the key and position columns are named	open	no source names the key and position columns	relations; system_instructions; tool_definitions; input_messages; output_messages; tool_call_arguments; tool_call_result; memory_records; retrieval_documents; parts
M17	a log record without trace and span ids is keyed by its position in the file	open	Content › Integrations › OTLP records (ids optional); no source keys it	relations
